<section class="v2-sec grey">
  <div class="v2-wrap">
    <div class="v2-head c"><span class="v2-eyebrow">Questions</span><h2 class="v2-h2">What do people ask about <em>Discovery Consultation?</em></h2></div>
    <div class="v2-faq">
      <details><summary>What does the Discovery Consultation include?</summary><p>A 1-hour telephone or in-person consultation, a full assessment of your relocation needs, a personalised move plan document, a recommended timeline and budget breakdown, and priority access to Chayce&rsquo;s full-service packages.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I have to book a full package afterwards?</summary><p>No. It&rsquo;s the natural starting point if you&rsquo;re not sure which level of support you need, with no obligation to book anything further.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How long does the Discovery Consultation take?</summary><p>It&rsquo;s a detailed 1-hour consultation, held either in person or by telephone.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What do I get at the end of the consultation?</summary><p>A personalised move plan document, along with a recommended timeline and budget breakdown.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Does the £150 count towards a package if I book one afterwards?</summary><p>Speak with your consultant during the call; they&rsquo;ll confirm how the Discovery fee applies if you go on to book a full package.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if I only need a straightforward move?</summary><p>If you already know your destination and just need packing and removals handled, you can go straight to Bronze Essentials instead.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Where does the Discovery Consultation take place?</summary><p>In person at our Northampton office on Kingsthorpe Road, or by phone, whichever you prefer.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What kinds of move is the Discovery Consultation for?</summary><p>Downsizing, a move into <a href="/retirement-village-removals/">retirement housing</a> or a <a href="/care-home-removals/">care home</a>, helping a parent move, a <a href="/moving-after-bereavement/">move after a bereavement</a>, or selling a family home and moving on. Whichever applies, you leave with a plan, timeline and budget.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I arrange it for a parent who lives far away?</summary><p>Yes. Moves are often arranged by adult children on a parent&rsquo;s behalf, by phone or video, and your coordinator keeps everyone updated.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I book a Discovery Consultation if the move is urgent?</summary><p>Tell us as soon as you know. We work to shorter timescales where we can, and a Discovery Consultation can set out a realistic plan.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I have a Discovery Consultation if I live outside Northampton?</summary><p>Yes. It can be held by phone, and we arrange moves across the whole UK.</p></details>
      
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

